## MutationObserver Setup

```typescript
// Always observe the chat container, not document.body
const chatRoot = document.querySelector('[role="log"]')
              ?? document.querySelector('[data-testid*="chat-window"]')
              ?? document.querySelector('[aria-label*="chat"]')

if (!chatRoot) return  // LiveAgent not loaded yet — retry on next mutation

observer.observe(chatRoot, {
  childList:       true,
  subtree:         true,
  attributes:      true,
  characterData:   false,          // don't observe text node changes — too noisy
  attributeFilter: ['data-status', 'data-resolution-status', 'aria-label'],
})
```

---

## Extraction Priority Order

Always try strategies in this order, stop at first match:

1. `role="article"` inside `role="log"` — most semantic
2. `[data-testid*="message"]` — LiveAgent's test IDs
3. `[aria-label*="message"]` — ARIA labels
4. Time-stamped `<p>` fallback — last resort

Never use:
- CSS class selectors (`.anything`)
- Tag-only selectors (`div`, `span`, `p`) without an attribute qualifier
- XPath

