## Encryption — AES-GCM via Web Crypto

```typescript
// vault.ts pattern
const KEY_STORAGE = 'cryptoKey'

export async function getOrCreateKey(): Promise<CryptoKey> {
  const stored = await chrome.storage.session.get(KEY_STORAGE)
  if (stored[KEY_STORAGE]) {
    return crypto.subtle.importKey(
      'raw',
      new Uint8Array(stored[KEY_STORAGE]),
      'AES-GCM',
      false,
      ['encrypt', 'decrypt'],
    )
  }
  const key = await crypto.subtle.generateKey(
    { name: 'AES-GCM', length: 256 },
    true,
    ['encrypt', 'decrypt'],
  )
  const exported = await crypto.subtle.exportKey('raw', key)
  await chrome.storage.session.set({ [KEY_STORAGE]: Array.from(new Uint8Array(exported)) })
  return key
}
```

Key notes:
- Key stored in `chrome.storage.session` — cleared when browser closes (intentional)
- Encrypted data stored in `chrome.storage.local` — persists across browser restarts
- Each encrypted chunk has its own random IV — never reuse IVs

